		{
			dependencies: ["34876F54406B6A04"]
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"Unlike &aRF power&r, which is safe to transport with &bPipez&r, &aEU power &erequires caution&r. Without proper attention, it is possible that your expensive wires, cables, or machines could be destroyed."
				""
				"EU is transported in &aamperes&r (&aamps&r), which can be thought of as packets of energy. The amount of energy stored in the packet is the &avoltage tier&r."
				""
				"The flow of power can be thought of as machines pulling power from the source through the cables. If a wire or cable is transporting too many amps or too high a voltage &cit will burn up&r, starting with its coating. Similarly, if a machine receives too high a voltage, &cit will explode&r. &eOn Hard/Expert modes, this explosion will break blocks!&r Be careful!"
				"Each voltage tier is &a4x the size&r of the previous tier, starting with 32EU/t at &7LV&r, 128EU/t at &bMV&r, 512 at &6HV&r and so on."
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: false
			hide_until_deps_visible: false
			icon: "gtceu:hpic_wafer"
			id: "46475B351ED6853F"
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.75d
			tasks: [{
				id: "080DCD71B7170FDB"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "A Primer on Power"
			x: -13.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
