		{
			dependencies: [
				"53347AAAE4495F95"
				"5D9399DD7DF6F153"
				"0381464BDF6B67E5"
			]
			description: [
				"&6Diodes&r are a component in the next Circuit tiers. They are made in an &3Assembler&r from liquid &9Glass&r, &6Fine Copper Wire&r and &6Gallium Arsenide&r. "
				""
				"Always be on the lookout for &ebetter recipes&r! &6Fine Annealed Copper Wire&r doubles your yield, and &9Polyethylene&r unlocks a few more efficient recipes."
			]
			hide_until_deps_complete: true
			id: "591A1B8B279DFCC9"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1FB54E4EC1F36941"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.75d
			tasks: [{
				id: "768DB070EA8F5B25"
				item: "gtceu:diode"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Diodes"
			x: 15.0d
			y: 7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"61AD3760E271B431"
				"5F109188BE4D9767"
				"35F9EC1A213BEDC7"
				"1DBBE96165C7987D"
			]
			description: [
				"&2Initial circuit components can be complex in GTm, as you need both Arsenic and Gallium.&r"
				""
				"For &9Gallium&r, you may, ranked from worst to best:"
				""
				"- &3Electrolyze &aSphalerite&r for a low chance of small dust. Note that you lose on direct smelting value."
				""
				"-&r Put &aCrushed Bauxite&r in the &3Chemical Bath&r. Note that this requires &9Sodium Persulfate&r. "
				""
				"- Obtain it as a Byproduct of &aSphalerite&r Ore Processing, in the &3Thermal Centrifuge&r or &3Centrifuge&r."
				""
				"&2For Arsenic, you must centrifuge Realgar Dust, or (more involvedly) flash smelt Cobaltite Dust in the EBF, and electrolyse the resultant Arsenic Trioxide."
				""
				"Combine both in a Mixer to make Gallium Arsenide."
			]
			id: "53347AAAE4495F95"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E9DED83C17EA29F"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.75d
			tasks: [{
				id: "2125B9BDF4FD7904"
				item: "gtceu:gallium_arsenide_dust"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&2Gallium Arsenide"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 12.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4A5CC6210FCEC075"]
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"When you first started the pack, we told you that ore processing can wait. Now, the wait is over. You need to start doing some rudimentary ore processing for &ebyproducts&r."
				""
				"Byproducts are additional materials that can only be obtained from processing ores in certain machines. For example, there is no \"Gallium Ore\" or \"Arsenic Ore\". You get &6Gallium&r and &6Arsenic &ras a byproduct from processing other ores."
				""
				"&cYour macerator must be HV or higher to make byproducts. Other ore processing machines do not have this restriction.&r"
				""
				"As such, your first forays into ore processing for byproducts will be the &3Electrolyzer&r, &3Ore Washer&r, and the &3Centrifuge&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&eFor the time being, raw ores should be crushed in a Macerator, washed in an Ore Washer, then smashed with a Forge Hammer before finally being separated in a Centrifuge.&r The resulting dusts can then be electrolyzed if needed."
				""
				"This ore processing route offers a good combination of byproducts without taking too much time to process ores."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:small_gallium_dust"
			id: "61AD3760E271B431"
			shape: "square"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{
				id: "5E6A27EC5AF00A4B"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&2Ore Processing for Byproducts"
			x: 5.0d
			y: 12.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5FE0B3C3179C22AB"]
			description: [
				"Ores have various means of processing, and eventually you'll use machine pipelines to process ores in specific ways to optimize what byproducts you gain. You can look at the &6Ore Byproduct Page&r of an ore in &bEMI&r, accessed by pressing 'U' on an ore and navigating to the byproduct tab, to see the required route to obtain desired byproducts. "
				""
				"The relevant machines are as follows:"
				""
				"- &3Macerator&r: turns ores into &6Crushed Ores&r, &6Crushed Ores&r into &6Impure Dusts&r, and &6Purified Crushed Ores&r into &6Pure Dusts&r. &eHV&r and above macerators have byproduct slots and gain a chance to get a full pile of byproduct from ores and both types of crushed ores."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"- &3Ore Washer&r: cleans Crushed Ores with &9Water&r, making Purified Crushed Ores&r, and a chance for a full pile of byproduct. Using &9Distilled Water&r makes them go faster. &2You can also perform a simple wash that is similar to Cauldron washing. It is extremely fast, but grants no byproducts.&r"
				""
				"- &3Chemical Bath&r: &2uses Sodium Persulfate or Mercury to purify certain ores, granting a chance to yield a full pile of a byproduct."
				""
				"- &3Centrifuge&r: separates Pure or Impure dusts into the final material, with a chance for a full pile of byproduct."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"- &3Electrolyzer&r: uses power to split compounds into individual elements, sometimes gaining useful byproducts in the process. &2Be warned that certain dusts may be better to directly smelt instead of electrolyze!&r"
				""
				"- &3Thermal Centrifuge&r: not to be confused with the regular Centrifuge. &2Less slow and power-hungry now, but still so. However, it yields a chance for byproduct, and macerating the Centrifuged Ore can grant a special third byproduct."
				""
				"- &3Sifter&r: &2filters high-quality Gems from Purified Crushed gem Ores for an overall higher yield."
				""
				"-&3Electromagnetic Separator&r: filters magnetic metals from certain ores, increasing their yields.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_ore_washer"
			id: "2B7B623879D6E94A"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{
				id: "0B7B0FFB3FEE3F79"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Ore Processing Machines"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6AE36CD4F39DAB08"]
			description: [
				"&3Centrifuges&r have a chance of creating additional materials when processing ore dusts. Sometimes it's the main dust, but often it's a different useful material that is otherwise unobtainable."
				""
				"Instead of washing &6impure dusts&r (made from macerating or hammering ores) in a cauldron, you can get more out of each dust by centrifuging it. The same is true of &6pure dusts&r, when you eventually make a &3Washer&r or &3Chemical Bath&r. Note, however, that pure and impure dusts will usually give different byproducts (always check in &bEMI&r)."
				""
				"Centrifuges also have other uses like unmixing compound dusts and fluids, or getting &6Rubber Pulp&r, which can be chemically reacted with &6Sulfur&r to efficiently make &9liquid Rubber&r."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_centrifuge"
			id: "5F109188BE4D9767"
			rewards: [{
				id: "42D617F339691CDD"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.75d
			tasks: [{
				id: "79E44B9FE48FA14C"
				item: "gtceu:lv_centrifuge"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Centrifuge"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"591A1B8B279DFCC9"
				"1F8B22B403FF3BF4"
			]
			description: [
				"Your first &6Tier Two Circuits&r will require three &6Tier One Circuits&r plus two &6Diodes&r."
				""
				"These are rather expensive. Always be on the lookout for a cheaper way to make your circuits — new sets of recipes become available each time you make a new tier of &2Circuit Assembler&r. Conveniently, this tier of Circuit unlocks one now!"
			]
			id: "3054D3CE8F49AB20"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4574DFB0E9D86375"
